; ============================================================
; FILE:        enterprise.mst
; MODULE:      Phase 4 — Packaging > Windows MSI Transform
; TASK:        T-053
; AUTHOR:      FocusMe Co-Pilot (Claude Opus)
; GENERATED:   Session 4
; PURPOSE:     Enterprise MST (transform) stub for GPO deployment.
;              Real .mst files are binary — this is a specification
;              document that defines the transform properties.
;              Use Orca or WiX to generate the actual .mst binary.
; ============================================================
;
; ENTERPRISE MST — Transform Property Table
; ==========================================
;
; This transform modifies the base FocusMe_x64.msi for enterprise
; deployment via Group Policy (GPO) or SCCM/Intune.
;
; Apply: msiexec /i FocusMe_x64.msi TRANSFORMS=enterprise.mst /qn
;
; ┌──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┐
; │ Property             │ Value                                │
; ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤
; │ SILENT_INSTALL       │ 1                                    │
; │ ALLUSERS             │ 1                                    │
; │ REBOOT               │ ReallySuppress                       │
; │ ARPNOREMOVE          │ 1  (prevent user uninstall)          │
; │ ARPNOMODIFY          │ 1  (prevent user modify)             │
; │ ARPNOREPAIR          │ 1  (prevent user repair)             │
; │ MSIINSTALLPERUSER    │ 0  (force per-machine)               │
; │ INSTALLDIR           │ [ProgramFiles64Folder]FocusMe\       │
; │ LAUNCH_ON_INSTALL    │ 0  (don't launch UI after install)   │
; │ REGISTER_CHROME_NMH  │ 1  (register Chrome NMH)             │
; │ REGISTER_EDGE_NMH    │ 1  (register Edge NMH)               │
; │ REGISTER_FIREFOX_NMH │ 1  (register Firefox NMH)            │
; └──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘
;
; USAGE SCENARIOS:
;
; 1. GPO Software Installation:
;    - Assign to Computer Configuration > Policies > Software Settings
;    - Add FocusMe_x64.msi with enterprise.mst as modification
;    - Installs silently at next computer startup
;
; 2. SCCM/Intune:
;    - Package: msiexec /i FocusMe_x64.msi TRANSFORMS=enterprise.mst /qn
;    - Detection rule: HKLM\SOFTWARE\FocusMe\WFP\Installed = 1
;    - Uninstall: msiexec /x {E8A3F4B1-7C2D-4E6A-9B5F-1D3A8C7E2F4B} /qn
;
; 3. PowerShell (manual):
;    - Start-Process msiexec -ArgumentList '/i','FocusMe_x64.msi',
;      'TRANSFORMS=enterprise.mst','/qn' -Wait -NoNewWindow
;
; TO BUILD THE ACTUAL .MST:
;
; Option A — Using Orca (Windows SDK):
;   1. Open FocusMe_x64.msi in Orca
;   2. Transform > New Transform
;   3. Modify the Property table with the values above
;   4. Transform > Generate Transform > Save as enterprise.mst
;
; Option B — Using WiX:
;   wix mst FocusMe_x64.msi enterprise.msi -o enterprise.mst
;   (where enterprise.msi has the property overrides above)
;
; Option C — Using msitran.exe (Platform SDK):
;   msitran -a enterprise.mst FocusMe_x64.msi
;
; SECURITY NOTES:
;
; - ARPNOREMOVE=1 prevents users from uninstalling via Add/Remove Programs.
;   Admin-level uninstall is still possible via msiexec /x with elevation.
; - The daemon service runs as LocalSystem and auto-restarts on failure.
; - EV code signature is verified during install (custom action).
; - WFP callout driver requires WHQL signing (separate from EV cert).
;
; ============================================================
